\title{Signed interior intersections}
\taxon{Definition}
\tag{definition}
\meta{defines}{signed intersection number}
\meta{dependencies}{[Normalized drawings](cn-0008)}
\meta{provenance}{[OpenAI, 23 September 2026](cn-0042), Section 3 before equation (3.1); reconstructed as a reading account on 9 October 2026. [Lean source: TruncatedSignedIntersections](/source-material/openai-math/lean/OAI/Combinatorics/Crossing/TruncatedSignedIntersections.lean).}

\p{For oriented edges #{e,f} in a [normalized drawing](cn-0008), give a crossing sign #{+1} when their ordered tangent directions have positive determinant in the oriented plane and #{-1} otherwise. Their \em{signed intersection number} #{I(e,f)} is the sum of these signs over all their interior crossings; set #{I(e,e)=0}.}

\p{Thus #{I(f,e)=-I(e,f)}, and #{|I(e,f)|} is at most the number of crossing points of that pair. A zero signed count need not mean that the edges are disjoint. This distinction is used explicitly in [the rank bound](cn-0035).}
